 <p>&gt; ⭐ **THE RULE THIS SECTION IS BUILT ON — THE PRODUCER&#x27;S OWN WORDING WINS. A renderer that rebuilds a fact is a SECOND PRODUCER, and two producers of one fact are two things that can disagree.** So a cell here prints what the artifact SAYS, not a sentence composed about it: the checkpoint identity comes from `provenance.ckpt.registry_key_display` (computed once by `taniteval.bench.contract`), a refusal prints the artifact&#x27;s own reason, a devkit line prints the producer&#x27;s verbatim string, and a number keeps the UNITS its artifact declares. ⛔ Three defects in one day came from breaking this rule in three costumes: a re-derived checkpoint key, an assumed `×100` that printed **2.9098 m as &quot;290.98&quot;**, and a composed `+ 1 patches` that replaced a line naming three. ⇒ **if you find yourself formatting a fact the producer already formatted, read its field instead.</p>
